kappa = 1/2 FITTED (never derived).  The mass is still required.  Nothing here says the theory is closed or that data favour it.

======================================================================================================================
S  sympy: closed forms and identities
======================================================================================================================
  [PASS] S1 A1 (Q = xi H rho_DE): rho_DE = Omega_L a^-xi and rho_c a^3 = Omega_c - xi Omega_L (1 - a^(3-xi))/(3-xi) solve the exchange equations
         measured: residuals 0, 0, 0
  [PASS] S2 A2 (Q = xi H rho_c): rho_c = Omega_c a^(xi-3), rho_DE = Omega_L + xi Omega_c (a^(xi-3) - 1)/(3 - xi); at early times rho_DE/rho_c -> xi/(3 - xi)
         measured: residuals 0, 0; limit 1/29
  [PASS] S3 A3 (Q = xi H_L rho_DE, H_L = sqrt(rho_DE) in H0 units): d(rho_DE^-1/2)/dt = xi/2, so a0(z)/a0(0) = 1/(1 + xi sqrt(Omega_L)(t_z - t0)/2) (CFG131's closed form)
         measured: residual 0
  [PASS] S4 G1 identity: d(rho_c a^3)/dln a = (Q/H) a^3, so rho_c a^3 constant on an interval <=> Q = 0 there (a transfer that keeps LCDM's a^-3 history exactly makes nothing)
         measured: residual 0
  [PASS] S5 B-pow: with rho_DE continuous (= Omega_L at z_t) and Q = xi H rho_DE (xi < 3) before z_t, the cold density created by z_t is xi Omega_L/(3 - xi) (a_i -> 0)
         measured: residual (xi = 1/2) 0
  [PASS] S6 B-step (sharp transfer at z_t with rate K H): created rho_c a^3 = rho_X a_t^3 K/(K - 3), i.e. the instantaneous bound rho_X(before) >= rho_c(z_t) is reached as K -> oo
         measured: residual 0 (K > 3)

