B, a0(z): after z_t rho_DE = Omega_L exactly, so a0(z)/a0(0) = 1 for all z < z_t (G2a PASS, G2b FLAT-LIKE) -- the framework's own constant rho_L,
  i.e. a PASS-AS-RESTATEMENT.  Before z_t, a0 ~ sqrt(rho_DE) would be sqrt(1/remnant) larger (2.27e+04 at z_t = 1100, 6.22e+11 at 1e8); no galaxies exist then,
  and the record's cosmology notes that a0 enters no linear coefficient (CFG4_cosmology.out header, XR26 part 1): not scored.

